case-study","dateCreated":"2021-07-26T21:39:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2021-12-22T20:19:47+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Intel Geospatial, a new venture from semiconductor chip manufacturer Intel, recently launched an open, cloud-based framework that uses artificial intelligence (AI) to visualize, analyze, and manage geospatial data collected by satellites, drones, and ground-based vehicles with sensors from Mobileye, an Intel company. Intel Geospatial’s focus is currently on electric utilities, oil and gas companies, city governments, and ecosystem service providers that lack big-data infrastructure. Using a software-as-a-service model, Intel Geospatial’s framework enables organizations to automate the inspection of infrastructure assets for maintenance issues—from damaged equipment and leaking oil tanks to missing traffic signs on busy city streets.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Intel-GeoSpacial%401x.aabc26615bd9ae1e14fb84828e97d9f9237cb6ec.png","displayLocation":"United States","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Electronics","sortDate":"2021-07-23","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/intel-geospatial-case-study/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2021","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Intel Launches Geospatial Data Management and AI Framework Using AWS","customer-name":"Intel Geospatial"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Lambda","description":"AWS Lambda","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:46+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#video","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Video",