","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)","description":"Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Storage","description":"Storage","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#orangetheory04282021lknadliaw","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"orangetheory04282021lknadliaw","dateCreated":"2022-05-23T21:42:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-05-23T21:53:05+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Orangetheory Fitness has over a million members around the world who rely on their signature Splat points and heart-rate based workouts to improve their health and wellness. In this special edition of This is my Architecture, join builder Liz Dennett as she explores how Orangetheory has been able to scale it’s studio based workouts and signature IoT hardware to create customized metrics to inspire and empower members. Discover how they have evolved their architecture and hardware to stream millions of data points from IoT devices while supporting unique needs of global members through Amazon Kinesis, DynamoDB, Lambda, and more.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/orange-theory_Logo%401x.46ef9e648be3dbfdf0e2416af87c799a33aae04a.png","displayLocation":"United States","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Professional Services","sortDate":"2021-04-28","headlineUrl":"https://youtu.be/DuxMG7RSBOU?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2021","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Orangetheory Fitness: Taking a Data-Driven Approach to Improving Health and Wellness","customer-name":"Orangetheory Fitness"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","ta