 data strategy.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-02-14T22:32:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-02-14T22:32:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#netflix-innovator","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"netflix-innovator","dateCreated":"2020-07-27T20:21:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-06-26T18:58:55+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","featureImageURL":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/aws-key-pages/homepage-key-pages/customer-stories-logo/Netflix.bfba696298d5edcd549b819e5abb2a766f816b36.jpg","descriptionSummary":"\u003cp\u003eNetflix is the world\u0026rsquo;s leading internet television network, with more than 200 million members in more than 190 countries enjoying 125 million hours of TV shows and movies each day. Netflix uses AWS for nearly all its computing and storage needs, including databases, analytics, recommendation engines, video transcoding, and more\u0026mdash;hundreds of functions that in total use more than 100,000 server instances on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Netflix_1x.4ae5e442fea7c25ec27b81891425de0b830cbfcc.png","displayLocation":"Americas","customerNameLower":"netflix","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eDelivering award-winning entertainment to more than 200 million members\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","industry":"Media \u0026 Entertainment","sortDate":"2019-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/netflix/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Netflix","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2019","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Netflix on AWS"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Kinesis","description":"Amazon Kinesis","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:45+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#c